area: config
case: 87-int-huge
verification: explicit-divergence
oracle: python
projection: config
reason: an OCaml int is 63 bits and the port's config holds every integer in one; Python's tomllib keeps arbitrary precision, and policy.max_snippet_chars has no upper bound, so tomllib accepts 2**62 and 2**70. The port refuses a value it cannot represent rather than truncating it. Closing the gap needs arbitrary-precision integers across the config surface — policy.max_snippet_chars is read as an int by the engine, the factory and the projection — so it is pinned as a platform limit and raised in the plan.
